Day 8 – Hybrid Demand Forecasting using Prophet and LSTM

Objective

The objective of Day 8 was to develop a hybrid demand forecasting model by combining the Prophet time series model with the LSTM deep learning model. The hybrid approach aimed to improve forecasting accuracy by leveraging both statistical and deep learning techniques.

Dataset Overview

The cleaned retail datasets (2009–2010 and 2010–2011) were imported and merged into a single dataset. Daily product demand was calculated by aggregating the total quantity sold for each transaction date.

Dataset Features

The forecasting dataset includes the following features:

- Date
- Demand

These features were used as input for both the Prophet and LSTM forecasting models.

Data Preparation

The Invoice Date column was converted into datetime format, and daily demand was calculated by grouping the Quantity sold for each day. The dataset was then divided into training and testing sets, with the last 30 days reserved for model evaluation.

Prophet Forecasting

The Prophet model was trained using the historical demand data. Future demand values for the next 30 days were predicted using Prophet's forecasting capabilities, capturing overall trends and seasonality.

LSTM Forecasting

The daily demand values were normalized using the MinMaxScaler. A sequence length of 30 days was used to prepare the input data for the LSTM model. The LSTM network was trained using PyTorch Lightning to learn temporal patterns in the historical demand data and generate future demand predictions.

Hybrid Forecast Generation

The final hybrid forecast was generated by averaging the predictions obtained from the Prophet model and the LSTM model. This combined approach utilized the strengths of both forecasting techniques to improve prediction performance.

Model Evaluation

The forecasting performance was evaluated using Mean Absolute Error (MAE). The MAE values of the Prophet model, LSTM model, and Hybrid model were compared to determine the most accurate forecasting approach.

Data Visualization

A line graph was plotted to compare the Actual Demand, Prophet Predictions, LSTM Predictions, and Hybrid Predictions. This visualization helped evaluate the forecasting accuracy of each model.

Forecast Export

The final forecasting results were stored in a CSV file named "hybrid_forecast_results.csv", containing the actual demand values along with Prophet, LSTM, and Hybrid predictions.

Key Findings

• Successfully merged the cleaned retail datasets.
• Generated daily demand data for forecasting.
• Split the dataset into training and testing sets.
• Trained the Prophet forecasting model.
• Developed and trained the LSTM deep learning model.
• Combined Prophet and LSTM predictions to create a Hybrid forecasting model.
• Compared forecasting performance using Mean Absolute Error (MAE).
• Visualized Actual, Prophet, LSTM, and Hybrid forecasts.
• Exported the final hybrid forecasting results for future business analysis.

Conclusion

Day 8 focused on developing a Hybrid Demand Forecasting model by integrating Prophet and LSTM predictions. The hybrid approach effectively combined statistical forecasting with deep learning, resulting in more robust demand predictions. The generated forecasts and evaluation metrics provide valuable support for inventory optimization, demand planning, and strategic business decision-making.